# Replayable boundary trace format: issue-542-protocol-correlation/v3
#
# Records are ordered exactly as written. The first column is monotonic elapsed
# time in microseconds. `transmit` and `frame` are engine inputs; `expect` is the
# corresponding state effect or observer-visible outcome. The final column on
# every expectation states the normative rule being frozen. Inquiry transmit
# records declare their payload shape; textual payloads are decoded fixture bytes.
trace issue-542-protocol-correlation/v3

scenario sony-exact-out-of-order-and-target-compatible
000000 | transmit | id=power-a target=1 kind=inquiry envelope=sony sequence=0x12340001 shape=unknown
000001 | transmit | id=zoom-a target=1 kind=inquiry envelope=sony sequence=0x12340002 shape=unknown
000002 | transmit | id=power-b target=2 kind=inquiry envelope=sony sequence=0x12340003 shape=unknown
000010 | frame | target=1 envelope=sony sequence=0x12340002 response=reply payload=0x2345
000010 | expect | observer=zoom-a outcome=reply:0x2345 | #542 exact Sony sequence matches are authoritative and target-compatible.
000011 | frame | target=2 envelope=sony sequence=0x12340001 response=reply payload=on
000011 | expect | observer=diagnostics outcome=ignored:target-incompatible-sequence | #542 exact Sony sequence matches are authoritative and target-compatible.
000012 | frame | target=1 envelope=sony sequence=0x12340001 response=reply payload=on
000012 | expect | observer=power-a outcome=reply:on | #542 exact Sony sequence matches are authoritative and target-compatible.
000013 | frame | target=2 envelope=sony sequence=0x12340003 response=reply payload=off
000013 | expect | observer=power-b outcome=reply:off | #542 decoded frames carry explicit target identity and the engine never recovers it from request bytes.
end

